{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>YHWH, I love the dwelling of Your house</b> — corresponding to 'I did not sit with men of vanity.'" "<b>And the meaning of 'Your house'</b> — for there are the righteous who serve Your name in truth, for there they sit always. Rabbi Moses said: for the meaning of 'Do not gather' is that he prays lest his end be like their end. And the correct view in my eyes: that plots not be fabricated that he associated with sinners all his days, and even with men of blood, who are worse than sinners."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:28:40.440630857Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}